In-game multiplayer (tools/web_wasm/net/sceneonline.cpp, netsync.cpp). The title's fourth entry
(the console's LAN MODE, which needs a broadband adapter the port does not have) is always offered,
drawn as MULTIPLAYER, and opens the multiplayer scene instead of SceneLanEntry (SceneFactory). In a
lobby room the host's START takes every member to the normal menus, which run in lockstep with one
controller per player: port_netsync_scene at each menu scene's init, the player count fixed to the
room's, VS only (no co-op: one kart per machine), the menus' wall-clock random seeds through
port_netsync_time. Course/map select hands the agreed race to netonline.cpp (port_net_race_begin
before RaceApp::call); every result-menu choice of such a race (also retry/replay) returns to the
multiplayer scene (RaceApp), and the VS result panel shows the local player when the winner is
another machine's kart (Result2D).

